# Git commits

Never write "by cursor ai", "Made-with: Cursor", "Generated by Cursor", Co-authored-by Cursor, or any similar AI attribution in commit messages, commit bodies, or git trailers.

Write commit messages as a human author would: concise, focused on why, matching this repo's existing style.

Always send a conventional commit message at the end of your response for the changes you made.

Never create a git commit yourself.
